  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Putting the second half of Katya's plan into action, Fedya corners Marina and kisses her right as Senya walks in. Furious at seeing his best friend kiss his wife, Senya explodes and chases Fedya across the room.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не понял, что здесь происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "А я тоже не поняла!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Он меня сам стал целовать!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Про какой-то ещё баркас говорил, Сень.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Рот закрой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вот денёк какой выдался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И друга потерял, и жену.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сеня, прекрати, помогите!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Сенечка, он сам начал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Ну всё нормально, всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Сенечка, милый мой, зайчик, послушай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Увольняйся отсюда сейчас же!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не понял, что здесь происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I do not understand, what is going on here?' The negative particle sits right before the verb meaning 'understood' to negate the statement.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "А я тоже не поняла!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I did not understand either!' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'understood' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Он меня сам стал целовать!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He started kissing me himself!' An emphatic spoken line centered on the verb meaning 'to become'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Про какой-то ещё баркас говорил, Сень.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He was talking about some boat too, Senya.' Gulya anchors the line on 'about', while 'Senya' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Рот закрой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Shut your mouth!' The grammar packs 'mouth' and 'close' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вот денёк какой выдался.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What a day this has turned out to be.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'here' and 'day' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И друга потерял, и жену.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I lost both a friend and a wife.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'wife'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Сеня, прекрати, помогите!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senya, stop it, help!' The meaning hinges on 'Senya' working together with 'help' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Сенечка, он сам начал!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senechka, he started it himself!' An emphatic spoken line centered on the verb meaning 'started'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Ну всё нормально, всё нормально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything is fine, everything is fine.' Notice how Russian expresses 'come on' and 'normally' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Сенечка, милый мой, зайчик, послушай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Senechka, my darling, little bunny, listen.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Senechka' before landing on 'listen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Увольняйся отсюда сейчас же!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Quit this job right now!' Senya brings out the contrast between 'quit' and 'from here' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
